WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.180
professor Dave here, let's talk about titration

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:16.359
acid-base titration is a way of determining how much acid or base is present in solution by determining the

00:00:16.359 --> 00:00:22.439
precise volume of acid or base that will
completely react with it. it's like a

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:28.740
kind of stoichiometry. on a titration
curve for an acidic solution, pH is

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.880
plotted against the volume of base that
is progressively added. as we add base

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:40.149
the pH slowly rises then sharply rises
towards the equivalence point. this is

00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:45.210
the point where precisely enough base
has been added to neutralize the exact

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:49.969
amount of acid in solution. when we
perform titrations we recognize the

00:00:49.969 --> 00:00:54.579
equivalence point by using something
called an indicator. this is a substance

00:00:54.579 --> 00:00:59.649
that will turn a vivid color once the
equivalence point has been reached. when

00:00:59.649 --> 00:01:04.299
we neutralize a strong acid with a
strong base the equivalence point will

00:01:04.299 --> 00:01:10.600
be 7. if either or both species are
weak this number will vary. for example

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:15.400
let's say there's a solution of sodium
hydroxide and we want to know its

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:21.020
concentration. we react 3.0M sulfuric acid with 25 mL

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:26.060
of the base and we find that it takes 11.6 mL of

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:31.020
acid to reach the equivalence point. if
we convert to liters and then have

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:35.909
conversion factors for the concentration
of the acid and then the stoichiometric

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:41.240
ratio, we can arrive at the concentration
of the reactants. let's check

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.300
comprehension

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.920
thanks for watching subscribe to my
channel for more tutorials and as always

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.130
feel free to email me

